I have created and saved the new **`youtube-video-studio`** skill.

### What This Skill Does

Whenever you want to brainstorm, write, or plan content for your YouTube channel, this skill will automatically:

youtube-video-studio
Generates YouTube Short and long-form video concepts, 5-topic angle selections, background research, and minute-by-minute scripts with visual storyboards. Use when the user asks to plan, script, storyboard, or outline YouTube videos, Shorts, tech/cybersecurity tutorials, or content ideas.

Instructions
YouTube Video Studio
A structured workflow to produce complete YouTube video packages for Shorts and standard long-form videos.

When to Use
Brainstorming YouTube video ideas or angles (5 curated options).
Developing scripts, background research, and reference links for a topic.
Generating a minute-by-minute or beat-by-beat storyboard with spoken audio, visual direction, and B-roll/overlay cues

Multi-Phase Workflow
Phase 1: Topic Selection (5 Distinct Angles)
When a user provides a niche, topic idea, or requests suggestions:

Provide 5 clearly differentiated angles/hooks, such as:
The Beginner Quick-Start: Accessible, clear, and reassuring.
The Myth-Buster / Threat Breakdown: High-stakes curiosity or debunking common errors.
The Deep-Dive / Comparison: Direct shootout between tools, methods, or devices.
The Actionable Checklist / Tutorial: Immediate step-by-step utility.
The Unpopular Opinion / Trend Forecast: Contrarian take on current trends.
For each angle, include:
Working title hook
1-sentence value proposition
Recommended format (Short vs. Long-form)
Pause or let the user choose which angle to flesh out. If the user already provided a specific topic, move directly into production for that topic.
Phase 2: Background Research & Media Links
Before scripting, assemble the context:

Core Knowledge & Key Facts: 3-5 technical points, facts, or security best practices that must be accurate.
Reference & Verification Links: Search terms or real sources for verification.
Visual Assets & B-Roll Suggestions: Suggested video clips, screen recordings (e.g. terminal, dashboard, hardware close-ups), stock footage, and graphics to run as overlays while speaking over them.
Phase 3: The Script & Storyboard Layout
Format the script based on the format chosen:

YouTube Shorts (30-60 Seconds)
Divide into fast-paced pacing blocks:

00:00 - 00:03 | Hook: High-retention question, bold visual, or curiosity gap.
00:03 - 00:15 | The Stakes / Setup: Why this matters right now.
00:15 - 00:45 | Core Value / Demonstration: The 2-3 essential steps or revelations.
00:45 - 00:60 | Payoff & Call-to-Action / Loop: Smooth loop hook or clear engagement question.
Standard Long-Form (Minute-by-Minute Outline)
Divide into timestamped blocks (e.g., 00:00 - 01:00, 01:00 - 02:30, etc.).

Storyboard Table Format

For every video, present the production plan in a structured storyboard table:

TimestampVisual Direction & OverlaysSpoken Voiceover / Audio ScriptVoiceover Cue00:00 - 00:30Camera on host talking to lens, lower-third graphic pop-in."Exact word-for-word text to speak..."Host on camera00:30 - 01:15Screen recording of tool dashboard with zoomed crop on settings."Exact word-for-word text explaining what is on screen..."Voiceover over video clip

Key Guidelines

Include precise cues for when the creator speaks directly to camera versus talking over external video clips/B-roll.
Keep spoken pacing natural (~130-150 words per minute).
Ensure cybersecurity, tech, and software explanations remain practical, safe, and accurate.